### 3. Planner — `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/plan.rs` + `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/cli/plan.rs`

`cli/plan.rs` (`PlanCommand::Approve{batch_id,actor}` / `Reject{batch_id,actor,reason}`, or bare `plan <design_docs...>` to generate). It loads config via `effective_repository_config`, resolves the repository identity via `FilesystemBacklogDiscovery`, opens the shared `database()`, and requires `config.planner` (`PlannerConfig`) to exist.

Core `plan.rs` API:
```rust
pub struct Draft { pub filename: String, pub content: String }
pub struct DraftSummary { pub filename, pub title, pub dependencies: Vec<String>, pub expected_files: usize, pub graph_width: usize, pub achievable_width: usize }

pub fn parse_agent_output(raw: &str) -> Result<Vec<Draft>, String>   // splits on "=== PRD-NNN.md ===" markers
pub fn validate_batch(root: &Path, drafts: &[Draft], limits: &PlannerConfig, excluding: Option<&Path>) -> Result<Vec<DraftSummary>, String>
pub fn generate(root: &Path, design_docs: &[PathBuf], config: &Config, paths: &AppPaths, db: &Database, agent: &dyn CodingAgent) -> Result<(String batch_id, Vec<DraftSummary>), String>
pub fn approve(root: &Path, id: &str, actor: &str, limits: &PlannerConfig, repository: &RepositoryIdentity, db: &mut Database) -> Result<Vec<DraftSummary>, String>
pub fn reject(root: &Path, id: &str, actor: &str, reason: &str, repository: &RepositoryIdentity, db: &mut Database) -> Result<(), String>
pub fn print_summary(id: &str, s: &[DraftSummary])
```
`generate()` writes drafts under `docs/prds/proposed/<batch-id>/`; `approve()` requires `human:<id>` actor (`fn human`), re-validates the batch (edits since generation are re-checked), rejects if any target filename already exists, records the decision via `PlannerBatchRepository::record(id, repository_key, "approved", actor, None, &hashes)` inside a DB transaction, then `fs::rename`s each draft from proposed → `docs/prds/`. `reject()` similarly records `"rejected"` with a non-empty control-char-free `reason`.

**Fake planner agent test double** (`plan.rs` tests, lines 761-943):
```rust
struct FixtureAgent(String);
impl CodingAgent for FixtureAgent {
    fn execute(&self, _: ExecutionRequest<'_>, output: &mut dyn io::Write) -> Result<ExecutionResult, AgentExecutionError> {
        output.write_all(self.0.as_bytes()).unwrap();
        Ok(ExecutionResult { exit_code: Some(0), ..Default::default() })
    }
}
```
Used as `generate(root.path(), &[design], &config, &paths, &db, &FixtureAgent(raw))` where `raw` is a string of `"=== PRD-001.md ===\n{content}"` blocks. `PlannerConfig { agent: Default::default(), max_prds_per_batch, max_bytes_per_prd }` is the minimal config; batch/human/approval assertions read back via `PlannerBatchRepository::new(db.conn()).get("batch-1")` (`.status`, `.file_hashes`).

Required PRD sections for a draft to validate (`REQUIRED` const, `plan.rs:20-28`): `Objective, Scope, Non-goals, Acceptance Criteria, Test Strategy, Expected Files, Definition of Done`, plus a `**Depends on:** PRD-NNN,PRD-MMM` or `**Depends on:** none` line. `validate_batch` also computes `graph_width`/`achievable_width` via `crate::drive::validate_claimed_width` (delegates to the scheduler's own conflict/width computation — same code path `drive` uses, see §4) and enforces strictly-increasing unclaimed PRD numbering and acyclic in-batch dependency ordering.

