### 5. Delivery — `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/delivery.rs` + `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/delivery.rs`

`DeliveryMode` (core, `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/delivery.rs:57-62`):
```rust
pub enum DeliveryMode { Disabled, ReviewedPrManual, PocSelfApproval, ReviewGatedAutomatic }
```
(`#[serde(rename_all="snake_case")]` → `"disabled" | "reviewed_pr_manual" | "poc_self_approval" | "review_gated_automatic"`; default is `ReviewedPrManual` when `mode` absent but legacy `enabled=true`, else `Disabled` — see `DeliveryConfigCompat::From` impl, lines 116-145, needed for FAM-BUG-023 backward-compat).

`DeliveryConfig` fields (line 9-53): `mode`, `enabled` (legacy), `max_deliveries_per_session`, `command_timeout_ms` (default 1_800_000), `remote`, `base`, `provider_argv: Vec<String>`, `auto_merge` (legacy), `staging_environment`, `deploy_argv`, `smoke_argv`, `rollback_argv`, `comment_blockers`, `required_checks`, `migration_gate_argv`, `credential_references`, `poc_warrant: Option<PocSelfApprovalWarrant>`, `review_gate: Option<ReviewGateConfig>`, `targets: BTreeMap<String,String>` (repository-local role → machine-local deploy-target-provider name).

`PocSelfApprovalWarrant { actor: String (must start "human:"), max_prds: u64, expires_at: String (RFC3339), assurance_label: String (must equal "LOW_ASSURANCE_POC_SELF_APPROVAL", the `low_assurance_label()` default) }`. `ReviewGateConfig { implementer, reviewer, approver }` — three *distinct*, non-empty identities required for `ReviewGatedAutomatic`.

`.validate()` (line 208-291) enforces mode-specific requirements: PoC prohibits `staging_environment` of `"production"`/`"prod"` and caps `max_deliveries_per_session <= warrant.max_prds`; ReviewGatedAutomatic requires the three distinct identities; both "automatically_authorized" modes (`.automatically_authorized()`, line 293) require non-empty `staging_environment`/`deploy_argv`/`smoke_argv`/`rollback_argv`.

`delivery.rs` core functions:
```rust
pub enum ConfiguredDeliveryOutcome { Environment{session_id,prd_id,role,target,revision}, Standard(DeliveryJournal) }
pub fn execute_configured(ownership_record: &Path, role: Option<&str>) -> Result<ConfiguredDeliveryOutcome, String>   // CLI-facing; `--to <role>` routes to deliver_to_with (environment/staging path), else `deliver`
pub struct DeliveryJournal { session_id, prd_id, worktree, branch, pr_number: Option<u64>, phase: String, detail: Option<String>, updated_at }
pub trait CommandRunner { fn run(&self, directory: &Path, argv: &[String]) -> Result<Output, String>; }   // <-- test seam
pub struct ProcessRunner { .. }  impl CommandRunner for ProcessRunner
pub fn deliver(ownership_path: &Path, policy: &DeliveryConfig) -> Result<DeliveryJournal, String>
pub fn deliver_with(ownership_path: &Path, policy: &DeliveryConfig, runner: &dyn CommandRunner) -> Result<DeliveryJournal, String>
pub struct TargetDeliveryResult { .. }
pub fn deliver_to_with(config, policy, role, repository_key, session_id, prd_id, revision, external_gates, conn, worktree, runner: &dyn CommandRunner) -> Result<TargetDeliveryResult, String>
```
`deliver_with`/`deliver_to_with` are journal-driven and idempotent/resumable — replaying with the same `.ownership.json`+`.delivery.json` never repeats an already-observed external side effect (see §6 burn-in tests below for exact assertions).

