### 6. Supervisor / launchd / systemd — failure injection and restart patterns

- `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/launchd.rs`: `pub fn plist(label, executable, repository, stdout_log, stderr_log, toolchain_path, restart_throttle_secs, max_prds) -> Result<String, String>` — pure renderer; validates label charset, all paths absolute, non-empty toolchain PATH, positive throttle/max_prds. Emits `KeepAlive.SuccessfulExit=false` (restart only on failure) and `ThrottleInterval` (restart throttling).
- `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/systemd.rs`: analogous `pub fn unit(label, executable, repository, stdout_log, stderr_log, toolchain_path, restart_throttle_secs, max_prds) -> Result<String, String>` — emits `StartLimitIntervalSec=300`, `StartLimitBurst=5`, `RestartSec=<throttle>`, `Restart=on-failure` (from `security_burn_in.rs` assertions).
- `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/supervisor.rs`: platform-neutral install/uninstall/status/validate:
```rust
pub enum Backend { Launchd, Systemd }
pub struct Spec { pub backend, pub label, pub definition: PathBuf, pub rendered: String }
pub struct Status { pub backend, pub definition, pub installed: bool, pub supervisor_state: String, pub blockers: Vec<String> }
pub fn detect() -> Result<Backend, String>                 // macOS→Launchd, Linux→Systemd, else Err
pub fn spec(executable, repository, paths: &AppPaths, config: &WorkerConfig) -> Result<Spec, String>
pub fn validate(spec: &Spec, repository: &Path) -> Result<(), Vec<String>>
pub fn install(spec, repository, log_dir) -> Result<bool changed, String>   // diffs+deactivates+rewrites+activates (launchctl bootstrap/kickstart or systemctl enable --now)
pub fn uninstall(spec) -> Result<bool, String>
pub fn status(spec, repository) -> Status
pub fn run_fixture(root: &Path) -> Result<String, String>   // harmless fail-once-then-recover fixture; NOT a real process kill
```
`run_fixture` (line 303-318) is the "harmless fail-once fixture proving restart recovery" used by `familiar-ai worker test` (`cli/worker.rs: WorkerCommand::Test`, lines 92-110): first call always errs (`"fixture requested failure restart"`), then writes `recovered`/`report` markers and succeeds idempotently on subsequent calls — asserted in `supervisor.rs`'s own test `fixture_fails_once_recovers_and_reports_once` and driven from the CLI which calls `run_fixture` twice more after the first failure and checks the two results are byte-identical (proving idempotent recovery + exactly one report).

**Real "process kill and restart" simulation** is *not* done by spawning and killing an OS process anywhere in this codebase's tests — instead the pattern is: (a) leave a durable `.ownership.json` with `state:"owned"` on disk (as if a worker died mid-attempt) and call `worktree::recover_incomplete(state_dir)` directly (§4 above), or (b) exercise `DriveTermination::worker_should_restart()` to prove the *session* reports a restart-worthy termination, or (c) invoke `familiar-ai worker run <repo> --max-prds N` as a **subprocess** (`cli/worker.rs:138-153`, which internally calls `drive_command` then `report_command` then returns non-zero if `worker_should_restart()`), and check exit code from `Command::new(env!("CARGO_BIN_EXE_familiar-ai"))`.

**Failure-injection/burn-in test file**: `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/security_burn_in.rs` (full text read above) is the direct PRD-037 precedent. Concrete reusable patterns:
- `RecordingRunner`/`AmbiguousCreateRunner`/`CommentCaptureRunner` implement `CommandRunner` to inject arbitrary failures/ambiguous results/hostile stderr into `deliver_with`, asserting exact external-call counts (idempotency: `ambiguous_pr_create_is_reconciled_without_repeating_external_effects` replays `deliver_with` after an ambiguous provider result and asserts each of `commit/push/create/view` ran **exactly once** total across both calls).
- `corrupt_delivery_journal_runs_no_external_command`: writes `<ownership>.delivery.json` = `b"{truncated"` then asserts `deliver_with` errors with `"invalid delivery journal"` and zero runner calls — fail-closed on corrupted state.
- `published_delivery_resume_skips_prior_external_effects`: writes a `DeliveryJournal{phase:"published",...}` directly and asserts resume goes straight to `"awaiting_merge_authority"` with zero new runner calls.
- `restart_storm_is_bounded_and_visible` / `supervisor_injection_is_rejected_or_escaped` / `supervisor_does_not_copy_ambient_secrets`: direct assertions on `systemd::unit(...)`/`launchd::plist(...)` rendered strings (throttle values, injection-safe escaping, no ambient env leakage even when `std::env::set_var` sets a canary before rendering).
- `hostile_provider_output_is_redacted_from_reports_database_rows_and_comments`: full `ReviewGatedAutomatic` delivery with a hostile `stderr` canary; asserts the canary is absent from `report::render(&db, None)`, from the raw SQLite file bytes, and from the PR "comment" call — this is the concrete "secret exfiltration" pattern relevant to PRD-038's failure-injection criterion.

