### 7. Morning report — `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/report.rs`

```rust
pub enum ReportError { NoSession, UnknownSession(String), Storage(String) }
pub fn render(db: &Database, session_id: Option<&str>) -> Result<String, ReportError>
```
Fixed section order (all in one string, redacted via `familiar_ai_agent::redact_sensitive`): header (`session/started/ended/termination/warrant/detail`) → `BUILT (n)` → `ESCALATIONS (n)` → `STOPPED (n)` (reason, workspace component/worktree/branch, adapter/model/exit/signal/phase, scope findings) → `AUTHORITY DECISIONS (n)` (only if any delivery decisions recorded; `mode/actor/decision/assurance/warrant_consumed`, `stop_reasons_json`, `findings_json`) → `RECOVERY` (`resumable/completed/blocked/skipped/invalid` counts + per-checkpoint phase lines) → `COST` (`known` micro-USD across N attempts / `unknown` count, never summing unmeasured as zero) → `CACHE` (`cached share`, `unmeasured`, `known savings`, `savings without pricing provenance`) → `NEEDS HUMAN JUDGMENT (n)` (special call-outs for `cost_unknown|storage_failure|delivery_blocked|budget_deliveries_exhausted|budget_tokens_exhausted`, then per-stopped-attempt exact `backlog release`/`backlog complete` command suggestions).

The rendering is **pure and deterministic** — same DB state ⇒ byte-identical output (proven by `rendering_is_deterministic_and_mutates_nothing`); the only non-constant content is stored timestamps, which the existing test `mixed_session_renders_every_section_byte_exactly` (report.rs:559-655) pulls from the just-recorded session row to build an exact expected string — this is the pinned-fixture-output pattern to reuse for asserting the multi-repo acceptance report deterministically.

Called from CLI at `cli/report.rs:6`: `crate::report::render(&db, session_id)` then `print!("{rendered}")`.

