## Summary

Implemented PRD-053 (Cost Reconciliation and Attributed Reporting) on top of the already-completed PRD-052 (Anthropic billing collection), PRD-055 (project attribution/usage_series), and PRD-064 (typed reservations).

**Storage layer** (`crates/familiar-ai-storage/`)
- Migration `054_cost_reconciliation.sql`: append-only `reconciliation_runs` + `reconciliation_rows` tables with a `current_reconciliation` view (predecessor-chain pattern, matching PRD-052's `current_provider_costs`), no-update/no-delete triggers.
- `AccountingRepository::reconcile_window(...)`: per-UTC-day matching of local `cost_estimates` against the current-effective provider projection, grouped by project (via PRD-055 workspace attribution bindings) or `unattributed`. Implements the closed status set (`reconciled`, `reconciled-with-variance`, `pending`, `mismatch`, `unattributed-provider-spend`), exact nanoUSD variance, tolerance/settlement-horizon policy, idempotent re-runs, and history-preserving re-opening on superseding provider revisions. Runs inside one transaction, so a crash mid-run rolls back atomically.
- `reconciliation_for_project`, `month_to_date_by_source`/`month_to_date_report` (per-source + aggregate that preserves source attribution), `accepted_prd_cost` (PRD-032 input, `authority: unknown` when no cost data exists — never zero).
- Reservation evidence is read-only (`resource_reservations` where `state='committed'`), never mutated — satisfies "reads settled reservations as evidence" without touching live warrant state.
- 9 new unit tests plus fixes to 8 pre-existing migration-count tests (expected, since 054 is a new tail migration).

**Config**: `ReconciliationConfig { tolerance_nanousd, settlement_horizon_days }` (defaults: 1¢, 3 days), documented in `config/default.toml`.

**CLI**: `billing reconcile <source> [--month]` (also auto-runs after `billing collect`), new `accounting month-to-date` / `accounting prd-cost` commands, `stewardship reconciliation <start> <end>`.

**Reporting**: morning report gained a byte-deterministic `RECONCILIATION` section (no wall-clock reads); `stewardship`/MCP/dashboard all expose project-scoped reconciliation reads with a `by_source` breakdown, cached-only, no network.

**MCP**: new `stewardship.get_reconciliation` tool, repository-scoped like its siblings.

**Tests**: 4 new daemon CLI-subprocess tests (`tests/cost_reconciliation.rs`) and 1 new MCP tool test, all against deterministic fixtures — no real provider calls.

One deliberate deviation from `expected_files`: `run.rs` was investigated but not touched — the live reservation-consuming warrant path already lives correctly in `drive.rs` (from PRD-064), and no functional gap for PRD-053's criteria was found there.

**Verification**: `cargo fmt`, `clippy -D warnings` (storage/mcp/daemon), and the full workspace test suite all pass — 65/65 test binaries green. The `familiar-ai-tray` binary can't *link* in this sandbox (missing system `libxdo`, pre-existing and confirmed on a clean checkout), so daemon/mcp tests were run with `--no-default-features`; `cargo check --workspace` confirms tray still *compiles*. One workspace-wide run also showed a single pre-existing, order-dependent flake (`paths::tests::tmp_fallback_uses_new_identity`) unrelated to this PRD — reproduced identically on the clean tree and passes reliably in isolation.

All acceptance criteria are implemented and covered by tests.
