# PRD-058 Codebase Investigation Report

Investigated at `/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788282372975203-0002412995-000000/PRD-58`. Organized by the 8 requested areas.

---

## 1. `crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/` — existing loop/runtime/adapter scaffolding

There is **no** raw-inference loop scaffolding here yet. Everything is built around synchronous, fire-and-forget subprocess execution of *external harnesses* (Claude Code, Codex CLI). This is the "harness" side of PRD-058's harness-vs-raw-runtime distinction — a new `raw_runtime.rs` (per PRD's `expected_files`) would sit alongside these as a new module, not replace them.

- **`lib.rs`** — crate root; re-exports the public surface (`CodingAgent`, `ExecutionRequest/Result`, `ClaudeCodeAgent`, `CodexAgent`, `isolated_command`, `WorkerRegistry`, etc.). Would need `raw_runtime` module + exports added.
- **`agent.rs`** (300 lines) — the core adapter contract for *harnesses*, not raw APIs:
  - `trait CodingAgent { fn execute(&self, ExecutionRequest, &mut dyn io::Write) -> Result<ExecutionResult, AgentExecutionError>; fn isolation_capability(); fn budget_capability(); fn preflight(); }` — this is a **blocking, single-shot, whole-execution** contract (spawn subprocess, stream stdout, wait). PRD-058's adapter contract (submit → streamed events → cancel) is a different, more granular shape and won't fit this trait directly; likely needs its own trait.
  - `BudgetCapability`/`BudgetDenomination`/`ExecutionBudget` — cost/tokens/duration ceilings per adapter, with per-adapter enforceability flags. Reusable vocabulary for PRD-058 ceilings.
  - `ExecutionRequest<'a>` — working dir, denied-read path, prompt, `prompt_cache_key` (stable-prefix cache identity — directly reusable for PRD-058's cache strategy), filesystem policy, model, timeout, budget.
  - `ExecutionResult` — token categories already split: `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `cached_tokens`, `cache_write_tokens`, `reasoning_output_tokens`, plus `Vec<ModelUsage>` for per-model detail (`uncached_input_tokens`, `cache_read_tokens`, `cache_write_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `reasoning_output_tokens`, `service_tier`, `provider_request_id`). This usage-category vocabulary is exactly what PRD-058's "distinct token categories" acceptance criterion wants and should be reused/extended, not reinvented.
  - `AgentExecutionError` — closed set: `Launch/Input/Wait/Output/MalformedOutput/Timeout/BudgetExceeded/BudgetStopped/UnenforceableBudget`. Analogous in spirit to PRD-058's closed stop-reason set but scoped to subprocess harnesses; PRD-058 needs its own closed enum (iteration-ceiling, token/context-ceiling, budget-stop, timeout, cancelled, provider-failure, fatal-tool-refusal, invalid-structured-output).
  - `redact_sensitive(String) -> String` — env-var secret scrubbing by name markers (SECRET/TOKEN/PASSWORD/API_KEY/CANARY) before untrusted text is logged/persisted. Directly reusable for tool-result/log scrubbing.
- **`claude_code.rs`** (1184 lines) — `ClaudeCodeAgent`/`ClaudeCodeSettings`, JSON stream-event parser (`parse_event`), cost/usage extraction (`parse_model_usage`, `aggregate_model_usage`, `hash_accounting_event` — sanitized-hash-not-raw-text pattern reusable for PRD-058 evidence hashing), `cost_to_microusd`/`decimal_to_scaled` (no-float decimal parsing, reusable pattern for cost normalization).
- **`codex.rs`** (683 lines) — `CodexAgent`, `CodexExecutionSession` (drive-session-scoped cache diagnostics), model-cache invalidation logic, its own `parse_event`/`stream_json`.
- **`isolation.rs`** (385 lines) — **the sandbox implementation directly relevant to PRD-058's "Authority and sandboxing" section**:
  - `isolated_command(executable, denied_read_path) -> Result<Command, AgentExecutionError>` — builds a `std::process::Command` wrapped in Landlock (Linux, allowlist-only via `pre_exec`) or `sandbox-exec` (macOS); unsupported platforms fail closed.
  - `build_landlock_ruleset`/`landlock_grant_paths`/`restrict_self_fully` — fail-closed, allowlist Landlock construction that denies a subtree and everything requires explicit read/execute grants.
  - `spawn_watchdog`/`finish_watchdog` — process-group timeout kill (`libc::kill(-(pid), SIGKILL)`), i.e. process-group cancellation already exists and is the pattern to reuse for PRD-058's "cancellation/timeout propagate to tool process groups."
  - Only denies read on one subtree today (used for reviewer isolation) — PRD-058 needs write-scope confinement to the execution's worktree and command allow/deny policy, which doesn't exist yet here.
- **`registry.rs`** (663 lines) — **this is PRD-057's leftover scaffolding**, the adapter-neutral routing layer:
  - `WorkerStage`/`WorkerCapability` enums (Planning/Implementation/Review/Remediation/NarrowTask).
  - `WorkerDescriptor` — `id, spec_identity, empirical_version, runtime_id, provider, model, executable, capabilities, fresh_process_isolation, context_tokens, estimated_cost_microusd, available, effort, permission_mode, extra_args`. **This is the PRD-057 worker-spec/runtime-id identity carried through to routing.** A raw-runtime worker (`anthropic-api`, `openai-api`, etc.) is expected to populate `runtime_id` with these values.
  - `trait AdapterFactory { fn adapter_id(&self) -> &str; fn build(&self, &WorkerDescriptor) -> Result<Box<dyn CodingAgent>, String>; }` + `AdapterFactories` registry + `builtin_adapter_factories()` (registers `codex`, `ollama`→Codex-OSS-adapter, `claude-code`). **A raw runtime adapter (e.g. `anthropic-api`) would register here as a new `AdapterFactory`** — but note `build()` returns `Box<dyn CodingAgent>`, i.e. today's blocking-subprocess trait; PRD-058's loop is a different execution shape (streaming, tool round-trips) so either `CodingAgent` needs a new raw-runtime-compatible variant/wrapper, or a parallel registry is needed.
  - `WorkerRegistry` — `register`, `add_rule` (operator route rules matched by `risk_classes`/`max_expected_files`, first-match-wins), `resolve` (id or legacy `provider/model` alias, ambiguous across runtimes on purpose — see `legacy_provider_model_pin_never_chooses_between_runtimes` test), `select` (deterministic lowest-cost-then-id tiebreak, full rejection-reason tracking via `RejectionReason`/`CandidateEvaluation`/`SelectionRecord`).
  - Extensive tests already assert PRD-057 identity separation (harness vs. raw-runtime spec identities never conflate).

**No** existing capability vocabulary for canonical tool capabilities (read-file/search/run-command/apply-edit/etc.) exists anywhere in this crate — that's wholly new for PRD-058.

