## 2. `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/` — the local OpenAI-compatible seam

- **`lib.rs`** — doc comment: "Local LLM manager + pluggable backends... v1 ships two backends: `StubBackend` and `OpenAiHttpBackend`... mistral.rs and true in-process inference are out of scope." Exports `LlmBackend`, `LlmError`, `BackendParams`, `LlmManager`, `InferenceRouter`, `HealthStatus`, `LlmHealthState`.
- **`backend.rs`** — `trait LlmBackend: Send + Sync { fn name(); async fn health_check() -> Result<HealthStatus,_>; async fn summarize(input, max_tokens) -> Result<String,_>; async fn classify(input, labels) -> Result<String,_>; async fn embed(input) -> Result<Vec<f32>,_>; }`. **This is a fixed-purpose (summarization/classification/embedding) trait, not a general chat/tool-calling interface.** It has no streaming, no message history, no tool definitions, no structured output, no usage/cost reporting.
- **`backends/openai_http.rs`** (606 lines) — `OpenAiHttpBackend`/`OpenAiHttpConfig` — **this is the "local seam" the PRD references**. Confirmed:
  - **Interface**: `new(config) -> Result<Self, LlmError>`, then `health_check`/`summarize`/`classify`/`embed`, each a single non-streaming `reqwest` POST to `/chat/completions` or `/embeddings` on an OpenAI-compatible base URL (Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp, vLLM, OpenRouter-compatible).
  - **Streaming**: **No.** Every call does `.json(&body).send().await` then parses `choices[0].message.content` from a full JSON response — no SSE/stream parsing exists.
  - **Tool calling**: **No.** No tool/function schema is ever sent in the request body; the JSON bodies are `{"model", "messages": [{"role":"user","content":...}], "max_tokens"}` only.
  - Config: `base_url, model_name, api_key (Bearer), max_concurrent_requests (Semaphore), request_timeout_secs, max_input_chars` (client-side truncation with `... [input truncated]` suffix).
  - Error mapping: `LlmError::Timeout`/`Transport`/`Backend`/`Config`; HTTP status → `HealthStatus::Healthy/Degraded/Unavailable` with reasoned strings (401/403→auth, 404→not found, 429→degraded/rate-limited, 5xx→server error).
  - **Test/wiremock seam**: confirmed — `wiremock::{Mock, MockServer, ResponseTemplate}` with `matchers::{header, method, path}`; every backend method has full wiremock coverage (health 200/401/403/404/429/500/connection-refused, summarize success/error/truncation, classify exact/substring/fallback match, embed success/empty/404, API-key header assertion). **This is exactly the wiremock seam PRD-058's test-harness section refers to for local-backend integration** — PRD-058's own tests should follow this same `MockServer`/`Mock::given` pattern but must add a genuinely streaming + tool-calling-capable client (this file doesn't have either), likely a new module (e.g. `attempt.rs` per the PRD's expected files) rather than extending `OpenAiHttpBackend` (whose contract is intentionally narrow per its own doc comment: "not tied to OpenAI itself — do not rename to GenericHttpBackend").
- **`backends/stub.rs`** — `StubBackend` (no network, deterministic canned answers) — a good pattern reference for PRD-058's "deterministic fake inference adapter."
- **`manager.rs`** — `LlmManager::new(BackendParams)`/`new_stub()` — lifecycle/health wrapper around a backend; doc says "backends should not own lifecycle state."
- **`router.rs`** — `InferenceRouter` — routes between "builtin"/"remote" managers per config, `choose_packer_profile`, `score_importance`; consumes `familiar_ai_core::config::{InferenceConfig, BudgetProfile}`. This `InferenceConfig` is scoped to the summary/rollup/packer subsystem, separate from PRD-057's `worker_registry` provider config — **do not conflate the two config surfaces**.
- **`heuristics.rs`** — `needs_model`, `heuristic_packer_profile`, `ImportanceScore`, `heuristic_importance` — pure heuristics unrelated to the agent loop.
- **`error.rs`** — `enum LlmError { Config, Transport, Timeout, Backend, ... }` (fixed small set).
- **`types.rs`** — `HealthStatus` (Healthy/Degraded(String)/Unavailable(String)), `LlmHealthState`.
- **`factory.rs`** — `BackendParams` (backend selection struct).

**Conclusion**: The PRD's "starting local seam" is real but minimal — a non-streaming, non-tool-calling summarization client with a proven wiremock test pattern. PRD-058's actual inference-adapter contract (streamed text/tool-call/usage deltas, cache controls, reasoning controls, structured output) has no existing implementation and must be built fresh, per the PRD's own expected file `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/attempt.rs`.

