## 3. `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config.rs` and `src/config/`

`config/mod.rs` defines `struct Config` aggregating ~20 submodules; relevant fields: `providers: BTreeMap<String, ProviderConfig>` (machine-global inference endpoints, no credential bytes), `worker_registry: Option<WorkerRegistryConfig>` (mutually exclusive with legacy `agents`), `agents: Option<AgentsConfig>` (legacy two-role config), `driver: DriverConfig`, `review: ReviewConfig`.

- **`config/registry_workers.rs`** (681 lines) — **the PRD-057 config schema, directly relevant**:
  - `AgentAdapterKind` (Codex/ClaudeCode/Ollama — closed today, will need a raw-runtime variant or the `runtime` string field used instead — see below), `AgentEffort`, `AgentPermissionMode`, `FORBIDDEN_AGENT_EXTRA_ARGS`.
  - `AgentEntryConfig` — per-role adapter/executable/model/effort/permission_mode/cost-token-duration ceilings/extra_args, with `validate()` enforcing adapter-specific field legality (e.g. effort/permission_mode only valid for claude-code) and reviewer never gets `bypassPermissions`.
  - `WorkerCapabilityConfig` (Planning/Implementation/Review/Remediation/NarrowTask — stage-eligibility vocabulary, `as_str()` kebab-case canonical spelling).
  - `RuntimeCapabilityConfig` — **the PRD-057 capability vocabulary**: `EditsFiles, ExecutesCommands, ReadsRepository, NativeToolCalling, McpClient, StructuredOutput, Streaming, ResumableSessions, ContextCompaction, PromptCaching, ImageInput, MaxContext, ReasoningControls, SandboxBehavior, RemoteOrLocal, UsageReportingCategories, CostReportingMode, ParallelToolCalls, DeterministicSeed`. This is exactly the runtime capability list PRD-058 needs to check (e.g. `NativeToolCalling`, `Streaming`, `StructuredOutput`, `PromptCaching`, `ReasoningControls`) when deciding native-tool-calling vs. schema-constrained templates.
  - `CapabilityProvenanceConfig` (Declared/Probed/Observed/Unknown) and `CapabilityProfileConfig { capabilities: BTreeMap<RuntimeCapabilityConfig, CapabilityProvenanceConfig> }` — capability profiles are named and referenced by workers (`capability_profile: Option<String>`).
  - `OllamaRuntimeConfig` — the **only** existing example of a closed, adapter-owned `runtime_config` extension (`host: Option<String>`) — this is the pattern PRD-058 should follow for provider-specific adapter extensions (Anthropic/OpenAI/xAI-specific fields must stay similarly isolated, matching the PRD's "provider-specific fields stay in adapter extensions" requirement).
  - `RegistryWorkerConfig` — `adapter (legacy)`, `provider`, `model`, `runtime: Option<String>` (**note: raw-runtime ids like `anthropic-api`/`openai-api`/`xai-api`/`ollama`/`llama-cpp`/`mlx`/`vllm` from PRD-057 are expected to flow through this free-string `runtime` field**, not a closed enum — `AgentAdapterKind` is legacy/harness-only), `model_artifact`, `auth_profile`, `capability_profile`, `runtime_config: Option<OllamaRuntimeConfig>`, `executable`, `capabilities`, `fresh_process_isolation`, `context_tokens`, `estimated_cost_microusd`, `available`, `effort`, `permission_mode`, `extra_args`.
    - `runtime_id()` — resolves `runtime` vs legacy `adapter`, erroring on contradiction.
    - `canonical_spec_identity()` — SHA-256 over `provider\nruntime\nmodel\nartifact\ncapability-profile` → `wspec-sha256:<hex>` — **the exact PRD-057 spec-identity algorithm**, directly reusable/must-match for PRD-058 evidence recording.
    - `empirical_version()` — SHA-256 over `(spec_identity, model_artifact, effort, permission_mode, context_tokens, extra_args)` → `wver-sha256:<hex>`.
    - `as_agent_entry()` — bridges registry worker → legacy `AgentEntryConfig` (only meaningful for harness adapters; a raw-runtime worker wouldn't go through this bridge).
  - `WorkerRoutingConfig`/`WorkerRouteRuleConfig` — pins per stage + operator route rules (risk_classes/max_expected_files), mirrors `registry.rs`'s `RouteRule`.
  - `WorkerRegistryConfig` — `workers: BTreeMap<String,RegistryWorkerConfig>`, `capability_profiles`, `routing`; `from_legacy_agents()` (lossless legacy→registry translation), `validate()` (non-empty checks, identifier validation, artifact sha256 format, `runtime_config` ownership restricted to `ollama`, risk-class vocabulary check, rule contradiction detection), `resolve_worker()` (id or ambiguous legacy alias).
- **`config/providers.rs`** — `ProviderConfig` (machine-global inference endpoint descriptor), `EndpointProviderKind`, `BillingMode`, `InferenceRuntimeKind`, `DeployRecipeConfig`, `AuthDescriptor` (external credential *references*, never bytes), `CredentialStoreDescriptor`, plus `validate_cloud_cli/host/ssh_host`. This is the machine-level provider registry (distinct from per-worker `auth_profile` strings which point into `auth_profiles`).
- **`config/review.rs`** — the PRD-013 config surface: `ReviewConfig`, `ReviewAgentConfig`, `ReviewTierPolicyConfig`/`ReviewTierConfig`/`ReviewTierRuleConfig`, `ScopeDeclarationModeConfig`, `ScopeClassPolicyConfig`, `ScopeFileClassName`, `ScopeFileClassConfig`, `ScopeClassificationConfig`, **`ReviewScopeConfig`** (this is the `review.scope` section), `SUPPORTED_CHANGE_KINDS` (7 git change kinds), `ProhibitedChangeConfig`/`TypedProhibitedChange`/`ResolvedProhibitedRule`, `validate_scope_path`, `ReviewVerificationConfig`.
- **`config/supervised_worker.rs`** — `WorkerConfig` (daemon-level worker supervision label/throttle/max-prds-per-run — unrelated to PRD-057 worker specs, naming overlap only).

**`config/default.toml`** relevant sections (line numbers from the file read):
- `[review]` (167–216): `enabled=false`, review attempt/cost/token/duration ceilings, `max_package_bytes/tokens`, `max_evidence_bytes`, `max_verification_log_bytes`, commented `prohibited_changes` examples with typed `path`/`class` rules.
- `[agents.implementation]`/`[agents.reviewer]` (195–216, commented) — legacy two-role config, closed adapter set (`codex`/`claude-code`).
- `[worker_registry.routing]` / `[worker_registry.workers.*]` (218–248, commented) — worked examples for `codex-primary` (runtime="codex", capability_profile="agentic-implementer") and `claude-review` (adapter="claude-code"); explicit note that "Ollama uses adapter = 'ollama'... invoked through the existing Codex OSS adapter path" — **confirms Ollama today is not yet a true raw runtime, it's routed through the harness path**, which is exactly the gap PRD-058 phase 4 fills.
- `[review.scope]` (260–274): `allow_prd_expected_file_expansion=false`, `declaration_mode="expected_or_configured"`, commented `[[review.scope.classification]]` example, `[review.scope.file_classes]` with defaults (`dependency_manifest/lockfile/migration/configuration → human_review`, `test → allow_when_expected`, `generated_artifact → human_review`).
- `[providers.unsloth-local]` (27–34, commented) — example of a machine-global inference provider descriptor (`kind="inference"`, `runtime="unsloth"`, `host`, `auth = "env: ..."`).
- `[driver]` (114–122) — session-level ceilings (`max_session_cost_microusd`, `max_session_tokens`, `max_session_duration_ms`, `max_concurrency`) — precedent for PRD-058's per-loop ceilings, though these are driver-session-scoped not per-inference-attempt.

No existing `[agent_runtime]` section exists — PRD-058's expected `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/agent_runtime.rs` and `config/default.toml` additions are net-new.

