## Summary

Implemented PRD-058 (Familiar-Owned Raw-Model Agent Runtime): a provider-neutral agent loop that composes prompts, offers canonical tool capabilities, validates/authorizes/journals every tool call, and records deterministic evidence and PRD-051 usage — tested exclusively against a deterministic fake inference adapter.

**New files:**
- `docs/contracts/agent-loop.md` — normative contract
- `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/attempt.rs` — provider-neutral `InferenceAdapter` contract + `FakeInferenceAdapter`
- `crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/raw_runtime.rs` — the loop core: canonical capabilities, validation, authorization (`ScopeAuthorizer`), write-ahead journal, evidence, closed stop-reason set
- `crates/familiar-ai-agent/tests/raw_runtime.rs` (12 tests) — full loop, tool round-trips, refusals, ceilings, cancellation, ambiguous-timeout usage, resume
- `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/agent_runtime.rs` — `[agent_runtime]` config, fail-closed validation
- `crates/familiar-ai-storage/migrations/055_agent_runtime.sql` + `repos/agent_runtime.rs` — append-only journal/evidence/attempts tables
- `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs` — SQLite journal, sandboxed executor (worktree-confined, env-scrubbed, process-group timeout kill), PRD-013-derived write-scope authorizer, PRD-051 ledger persistence, resume reconciliation
- `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/raw_runtime.rs` (10 tests) — persistence, scope refusal, command sandbox, real timeout kill, resume readiness

**Modified:** `lib.rs`/`Cargo.toml` wiring across 4 crates, `isolation.rs` (widened two existing functions from `pub(crate)` to `pub` for reuse), `config/default.toml`, `migrate.rs` (registered migration 55, updated 8 tests pinning exact migration counts/lists).

**Verification:** `cargo fmt --check` clean; clippy clean on every touched crate (two pre-existing, unrelated lint failures in `bootstrap.rs`/`summary_worker.rs` confirmed via `git stash` to predate this change); full `cargo test --workspace` green (one transient flake in an unrelated pre-existing subprocess-timeout test under heavy parallel load, non-reproducible across 5 reruns).

All 16 acceptance criteria are met. One is satisfied structurally rather than by an explicit runtime check: `ScopeAuthorizer::authorize` receives `AuthorityContext` (project/execution/worker binding) but doesn't compare it against a bound value, since each authorizer instance is already constructed per-execution — cross-execution binding can't leak through this path, but a future PRD wiring multiple executions through one shared authorizer instance should add that explicit check.
